node.doctext:
Hi Monks!<br><br>

From this simple code example, how  could I get all the keys  from the value "red"?
I thought using the "grep" command I could get the "apple" and "kiwi" from the hash, only getting "kiwi".<br>
Any simple suggestions?<br>

<code>
#!/usr/bin/perl


my $search = "red";

my %fruit = (
   'apple' => ['red','green'],
   'kiwi' => 'green',
   'banana' => 'yellow',
  );


my ($match) = grep { $fruit{$_} eq $search } keys %fruit;

print "\n\n Match = $match\n\n";
</code><br>
Thank you!
